{"id": "EUVD-2026-93167", "enisaUuid": "23d6b35b-b4d6-3921-bfbc-21fdc6bf94ac", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: lan743x: fix RX checksum use-after-free\n\nlan743x_rx_process_buffer() adds each non-first receive buffer to the\nhead skb's frag_list.  On the last descriptor, lan743x_rx_trim_skb()\nlinearizes the head and frees the fragment skb metadata.\n\nThe checksum-success path then writes ip_summed through the local skb\npointer, which still points to the final fragment.  This causes a\nuse-after-free write when a packet spans more than one receive buffer.\n\nSet ip_summed on the surviving head skb instead.  Multi-buffer receive\ncan occur after a live MTU increase because existing ring entries keep\ntheir old buffer size until they are replenished.\n\nA KUnit test invoking lan743x_rx_process_buffer() with a two-buffer\npacket produced a one-byte KASAN use-after-free write before this change.\nThe same test passed after the change.  The driver object also builds\nwith W=1.  This was not tested on physical LAN743x hardware.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:10", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e52886c4324c9897c2c62f92be3dc8316cee67e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a58024835c704419bb46d2a34e5223f65605f958", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6fe5c3a2503983abb431d93faeadfc7f5e6a7e33", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c216bfa9fb7b36804485e67975e9c98055b31ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/161a403c8625e152de03d1da22bbf9cda6dc9f9f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9ce4053dc945c5372dedba5017ee675b30dc0c5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98239", "GHSA-qcgj-xcvr-2727"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07ed19e2-6c84-3120-a760-5b48807c6572", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "13b28ae6-27b9-38dc-b17c-81e08b66412b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd6910501cfd9a3bdff2f5fc33c9f3cf165ca54a <161a403c8625e152de03d1da22bbf9cda6dc9f9f"}, {"id": "23ebb611-ea0f-3fb4-9794-1c9678675bf4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "5700e3db-bcde-30f5-a5cc-503e77e05368", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "5b707dfa-6a4c-30e3-9ede-0b14a69276e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "71f4def8-7e4a-30ed-b67c-d130479ae1d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd6910501cfd9a3bdff2f5fc33c9f3cf165ca54a <0e52886c4324c9897c2c62f92be3dc8316cee67e"}, {"id": "93268659-6ecf-3452-b20f-58e4ccb18dc5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd6910501cfd9a3bdff2f5fc33c9f3cf165ca54a <a58024835c704419bb46d2a34e5223f65605f958"}, {"id": "9ba43e24-6338-3620-b5db-9192e2ea8e4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "a53ba849-b527-39ae-b137-35643a1aa480", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd6910501cfd9a3bdff2f5fc33c9f3cf165ca54a <5c216bfa9fb7b36804485e67975e9c98055b31ef"}, {"id": "acd9d219-8f25-3650-a72e-771baa61b46e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "b77b0868-118a-389f-b56d-837f13513d54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd6910501cfd9a3bdff2f5fc33c9f3cf165ca54a <6fe5c3a2503983abb431d93faeadfc7f5e6a7e33"}, {"id": "c224b2ca-550b-390e-956f-f439976116b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "d8886614-3756-3941-90b4-bd35762f643c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "v